### name: rel.link.promotion.per-pair.a-left-field-the-first-element-lacks
--- note
Spec §7.4 promotes "the left element's scalar fields": each joined row takes
the fields of the left element it was built from. The second element has a
`tier` the first lacks; its row carries it. Every host computed the promoted
fields once, from the first left and first right element (SEL-0053).
--- source
X = LIST(RECORD("k", 1, "name", "a"), RECORD("k", 1, "tier", "P", "name", "b")); Y = LIST(RECORD("id", 1, "sku", "s")); J = X .> LINK(Y, _1["k"] == _2["id"]); J .> MAP(INDEXES(_))
--- expect
tree -{"1"=-{"1"=t"X", "2"=t"x", "3"=t"_1", "4"=t"Y", "5"=t"y", "6"=t"_2", "7"=t"k", "8"=t"name", "9"=t"id", "10"=t"sku"}, "2"=-{"1"=t"X", "2"=t"x", "3"=t"_1", "4"=t"Y", "5"=t"y", "6"=t"_2", "7"=t"k", "8"=t"tier", "9"=t"name", "10"=t"id", "11"=t"sku"}}
===
### name: rel.link.promotion.per-pair.a-left-field-this-element-lacks
--- note
The first element has a `tier`, the second does not: the second row has no
`tier` -- not a NULL one.
--- source
X = LIST(RECORD("k", 1, "tier", "P"), RECORD("k", 1, "name", "b")); Y = LIST(RECORD("id", 1, "sku", "s")); J = X .> LINK(Y, _1["k"] == _2["id"]); J .> MAP(INDEXES(_))
--- expect
tree -{"1"=-{"1"=t"X", "2"=t"x", "3"=t"_1", "4"=t"Y", "5"=t"y", "6"=t"_2", "7"=t"k", "8"=t"tier", "9"=t"id", "10"=t"sku"}, "2"=-{"1"=t"X", "2"=t"x", "3"=t"_1", "4"=t"Y", "5"=t"y", "6"=t"_2", "7"=t"k", "8"=t"name", "9"=t"id", "10"=t"sku"}}
===
### name: rel.link.promotion.per-pair.each-element-keeps-its-own-field-order
--- note
Promoted fields follow the order of the element they come from.
--- source
X = LIST(RECORD("k", 1, "a", 1, "b", 2), RECORD("b", 3, "k", 1, "a", 4)); Y = LIST(RECORD("id", 1)); J = X .> LINK(Y, _1["k"] == _2["id"]); J .> MAP(INDEXES(_))
--- expect
tree -{"1"=-{"1"=t"X", "2"=t"x", "3"=t"_1", "4"=t"Y", "5"=t"y", "6"=t"_2", "7"=t"k", "8"=t"a", "9"=t"b", "10"=t"id"}, "2"=-{"1"=t"X", "2"=t"x", "3"=t"_1", "4"=t"Y", "5"=t"y", "6"=t"_2", "7"=t"b", "8"=t"k", "9"=t"a", "10"=t"id"}}
===
### name: rel.link.promotion.per-pair.a-right-field-the-first-element-lacks
--- note
The right side the same way: the second right element's `sku` is promoted
onto the row built from it.
--- source
X = LIST(RECORD("k", 1)); Y = LIST(RECORD("id", 1, "name", "n"), RECORD("id", 1, "sku", "s")); J = X .> LINK(Y, _1["k"] == _2["id"]); J .> MAP(INDEXES(_))
--- expect
tree -{"1"=-{"1"=t"X", "2"=t"x", "3"=t"_1", "4"=t"Y", "5"=t"y", "6"=t"_2", "7"=t"k", "8"=t"id", "9"=t"name"}, "2"=-{"1"=t"X", "2"=t"x", "3"=t"_1", "4"=t"Y", "5"=t"y", "6"=t"_2", "7"=t"k", "8"=t"id", "9"=t"sku"}}
===
### name: rel.link.promotion.per-pair.a-clash-is-this-pairs
--- note
A name both elements of THIS pair carry is promoted from neither; a name
only some other right element carries does not stop the left field. The
first row clashes on `tier`, the second does not.
--- source
X = LIST(RECORD("k", 1, "tier", "L")); Y = LIST(RECORD("id", 1, "tier", "R1"), RECORD("id", 1, "sku", "s")); J = X .> LINK(Y, _1["k"] == _2["id"]); J .> MAP(INDEXES(_))
--- expect
tree -{"1"=-{"1"=t"X", "2"=t"x", "3"=t"_1", "4"=t"Y", "5"=t"y", "6"=t"_2", "7"=t"k", "8"=t"id"}, "2"=-{"1"=t"X", "2"=t"x", "3"=t"_1", "4"=t"Y", "5"=t"y", "6"=t"_2", "7"=t"k", "8"=t"tier", "9"=t"id", "10"=t"sku"}}
===
### name: rel.link.promotion.per-pair.a-clash-ignores-case
--- note
Names clash ASCII-case-insensitively, pair by pair: `Name` on the left and
`name` on the first right element hide each other; the second right element
has neither.
--- source
X = LIST(RECORD("k", 1, "Name", "L")); Y = LIST(RECORD("id", 1, "name", "r"), RECORD("id", 1, "amt", 5)); J = X .> LINK(Y, _1["k"] == _2["id"]); J .> MAP(INDEXES(_))
--- expect
tree -{"1"=-{"1"=t"X", "2"=t"x", "3"=t"_1", "4"=t"Y", "5"=t"y", "6"=t"_2", "7"=t"k", "8"=t"id"}, "2"=-{"1"=t"X", "2"=t"x", "3"=t"_1", "4"=t"Y", "5"=t"y", "6"=t"_2", "7"=t"k", "8"=t"Name", "9"=t"id", "10"=t"amt"}}
===
### name: rel.link.promotion.per-pair.a-null-right-field-is-this-pairs
--- note
A right field is promoted when it is not NULL in the right element of the
pair: NULL in the first, `"s"` in the second.
--- source
X = LIST(RECORD("k", 1)); Y = LIST(RECORD("id", 1, "sku", NULL), RECORD("id", 1, "sku", "s")); J = X .> LINK(Y, _1["k"] == _2["id"]); J .> MAP(LIST(INDEXES(_), _["sku"] ?? "absent"))
--- expect
tree -{"1"=-{"1"=-{"1"=t"X", "2"=t"x", "3"=t"_1", "4"=t"Y", "5"=t"y", "6"=t"_2", "7"=t"k", "8"=t"id"}, "2"=t"absent"}, "2"=-{"1"=-{"1"=t"X", "2"=t"x", "3"=t"_1", "4"=t"Y", "5"=t"y", "6"=t"_2", "7"=t"k", "8"=t"id", "9"=t"sku"}, "2"=t"s"}}
===
### name: rel.link.promotion.per-pair.a-null-left-field-is-promoted
--- note
A left scalar field is promoted whatever its value, NULL included -- only
the right side's NULLs are left out (§7.4).
--- source
X = LIST(RECORD("k", 1, "tier", NULL)); Y = LIST(RECORD("id", 1)); J = X .> LINK(Y, _1["k"] == _2["id"]); J .> MAP(LIST(INDEXES(_), HAS(_, "tier")))
--- expect
tree -{"1"=-{"1"=-{"1"=t"X", "2"=t"x", "3"=t"_1", "4"=t"Y", "5"=t"y", "6"=t"_2", "7"=t"k", "8"=t"tier", "9"=t"id"}, "2"=TRUE}}
===
### name: rel.link.promotion.per-pair.nested-or-scalar-is-each-elements
--- note
Whether a field is a nested record (carried first) or a scalar (promoted) is
decided per element: `m` holds a record in the first element and a number in
the second.
--- source
X = LIST(RECORD("k", 1, "m", RECORD("x", 1)), RECORD("k", 1, "m", 7)); Y = LIST(RECORD("id", 1)); J = X .> LINK(Y, _1["k"] == _2["id"]); J .> MAP(INDEXES(_))
--- expect
tree -{"1"=-{"1"=t"m", "2"=t"X", "3"=t"x", "4"=t"_1", "5"=t"Y", "6"=t"y", "7"=t"_2", "8"=t"k", "9"=t"id"}, "2"=-{"1"=t"X", "2"=t"x", "3"=t"_1", "4"=t"Y", "5"=t"y", "6"=t"_2", "7"=t"k", "8"=t"m", "9"=t"id"}}
===
### name: rel.link.promotion.per-pair.list-and-boolean-fields-are-scalar
--- note
Only a record with fields is a nested record; a list, a boolean and a text
are scalar fields and promoted.
--- source
X = LIST(RECORD("k", 1, "l", LIST(1, 2), "b", TRUE)); Y = LIST(RECORD("id", 1, "r", LIST(3))); J = X .> LINK(Y, _1["k"] == _2["id"]); J .> MAP(LIST(INDEXES(_), _["l"], _["b"], _["r"]))
--- expect
tree -{"1"=-{"1"=-{"1"=t"X", "2"=t"x", "3"=t"_1", "4"=t"Y", "5"=t"y", "6"=t"_2", "7"=t"k", "8"=t"l", "9"=t"b", "10"=t"id", "11"=t"r"}, "2"=-{"1"=t"1", "2"=t"2"}, "3"=TRUE, "4"=-{"1"=t"3"}}}
===
### name: rel.link.promotion.per-pair.a-run-of-matches-is-built-pair-by-pair
--- note
One left element meets a run of right elements of one shape whose `v` is a
text, NULL, a text, a record, a list, an empty record and a boolean: each
row promotes `v` or not from its own pair, and a pair that breaks the run
does not change the rows after it. An implementation that builds a left
row's matches in one loop (Python's, SEL-0056) sends a pair that breaks the
run the general way and picks the run up again after it.
--- source
X = LIST(RECORD("k", 1, "a", "x")); Y = LIST(RECORD("id", 1, "v", "t"), RECORD("id", 1, "v", NULL), RECORD("id", 1, "v", "u"), RECORD("id", 1, "v", RECORD("q", 1)), RECORD("id", 1, "v", LIST(2)), RECORD("id", 1, "v", RECORD()), RECORD("id", 1, "v", FALSE)); J = X .> LINK(Y, _1["k"] == _2["id"]); J .> MAP(LIST(INDEXES(_), _["v"] ?? "absent"))
--- expect
tree -{"1"=-{"1"=-{"1"=t"X", "2"=t"x", "3"=t"_1", "4"=t"Y", "5"=t"y", "6"=t"_2", "7"=t"k", "8"=t"a", "9"=t"id", "10"=t"v"}, "2"=t"t"}, "2"=-{"1"=-{"1"=t"X", "2"=t"x", "3"=t"_1", "4"=t"Y", "5"=t"y", "6"=t"_2", "7"=t"k", "8"=t"a", "9"=t"id"}, "2"=t"absent"}, "3"=-{"1"=-{"1"=t"X", "2"=t"x", "3"=t"_1", "4"=t"Y", "5"=t"y", "6"=t"_2", "7"=t"k", "8"=t"a", "9"=t"id", "10"=t"v"}, "2"=t"u"}, "4"=-{"1"=-{"1"=t"X", "2"=t"x", "3"=t"_1", "4"=t"Y", "5"=t"y", "6"=t"_2", "7"=t"k", "8"=t"a", "9"=t"id"}, "2"=t"absent"}, "5"=-{"1"=-{"1"=t"X", "2"=t"x", "3"=t"_1", "4"=t"Y", "5"=t"y", "6"=t"_2", "7"=t"k", "8"=t"a", "9"=t"id", "10"=t"v"}, "2"=-{"1"=t"2"}}, "6"=-{"1"=-{"1"=t"X", "2"=t"x", "3"=t"_1", "4"=t"Y", "5"=t"y", "6"=t"_2", "7"=t"k", "8"=t"a", "9"=t"id"}, "2"=t"absent"}, "7"=-{"1"=-{"1"=t"X", "2"=t"x", "3"=t"_1", "4"=t"Y", "5"=t"y", "6"=t"_2", "7"=t"k", "8"=t"a", "9"=t"id", "10"=t"v"}, "2"=FALSE}}
===
### name: rel.link.promotion.per-pair.runs-of-matches-under-left-elements-that-differ
--- note
Four left elements, `m` a record, a number, NULL and a record again, each
meeting the same three right elements, `s` a text, NULL, a text: the
nested-or-scalar fact is each left element's, and the NULL-or-not fact each
pair's, through every run.
--- source
X = LIST(RECORD("k", 1, "m", RECORD("x", 1)), RECORD("k", 1, "m", 7), RECORD("k", 1, "m", NULL), RECORD("k", 1, "m", RECORD("x", 2))); Y = LIST(RECORD("id", 1, "s", "a"), RECORD("id", 1, "s", NULL), RECORD("id", 1, "s", "b")); J = X .> LINK(Y, _1["k"] == _2["id"]); J .> MAP(LIST(INDEXES(_), _["s"] ?? "absent"))
--- expect
tree -{"1"=-{"1"=-{"1"=t"m", "2"=t"X", "3"=t"x", "4"=t"_1", "5"=t"Y", "6"=t"y", "7"=t"_2", "8"=t"k", "9"=t"id", "10"=t"s"}, "2"=t"a"}, "2"=-{"1"=-{"1"=t"m", "2"=t"X", "3"=t"x", "4"=t"_1", "5"=t"Y", "6"=t"y", "7"=t"_2", "8"=t"k", "9"=t"id"}, "2"=t"absent"}, "3"=-{"1"=-{"1"=t"m", "2"=t"X", "3"=t"x", "4"=t"_1", "5"=t"Y", "6"=t"y", "7"=t"_2", "8"=t"k", "9"=t"id", "10"=t"s"}, "2"=t"b"}, "4"=-{"1"=-{"1"=t"X", "2"=t"x", "3"=t"_1", "4"=t"Y", "5"=t"y", "6"=t"_2", "7"=t"k", "8"=t"m", "9"=t"id", "10"=t"s"}, "2"=t"a"}, "5"=-{"1"=-{"1"=t"X", "2"=t"x", "3"=t"_1", "4"=t"Y", "5"=t"y", "6"=t"_2", "7"=t"k", "8"=t"m", "9"=t"id"}, "2"=t"absent"}, "6"=-{"1"=-{"1"=t"X", "2"=t"x", "3"=t"_1", "4"=t"Y", "5"=t"y", "6"=t"_2", "7"=t"k", "8"=t"m", "9"=t"id", "10"=t"s"}, "2"=t"b"}, "7"=-{"1"=-{"1"=t"X", "2"=t"x", "3"=t"_1", "4"=t"Y", "5"=t"y", "6"=t"_2", "7"=t"k", "8"=t"m", "9"=t"id", "10"=t"s"}, "2"=t"a"}, "8"=-{"1"=-{"1"=t"X", "2"=t"x", "3"=t"_1", "4"=t"Y", "5"=t"y", "6"=t"_2", "7"=t"k", "8"=t"m", "9"=t"id"}, "2"=t"absent"}, "9"=-{"1"=-{"1"=t"X", "2"=t"x", "3"=t"_1", "4"=t"Y", "5"=t"y", "6"=t"_2", "7"=t"k", "8"=t"m", "9"=t"id", "10"=t"s"}, "2"=t"b"}, "10"=-{"1"=-{"1"=t"m", "2"=t"X", "3"=t"x", "4"=t"_1", "5"=t"Y", "6"=t"y", "7"=t"_2", "8"=t"k", "9"=t"id", "10"=t"s"}, "2"=t"a"}, "11"=-{"1"=-{"1"=t"m", "2"=t"X", "3"=t"x", "4"=t"_1", "5"=t"Y", "6"=t"y", "7"=t"_2", "8"=t"k", "9"=t"id"}, "2"=t"absent"}, "12"=-{"1"=-{"1"=t"m", "2"=t"X", "3"=t"x", "4"=t"_1", "5"=t"Y", "6"=t"y", "7"=t"_2", "8"=t"k", "9"=t"id", "10"=t"s"}, "2"=t"b"}}
===
### name: rel.link-left.null-record-is-shaped-like-the-first-right-element
--- note
An unmatched row's right binders hold "a record shaped like the right
elements whose every field is NULL": with elements of different shapes,
shaped like the first, as bound (with its name keys).
--- source
X = LIST(RECORD("k", 9, "tier", "L")); Y = LIST(RECORD("id", 1, "sku", "s"), RECORD("id", 2, "tier", "t", "name", "n")); J = X .> LINK_LEFT(Y, _1["k"] == _2["id"]); J .> MAP(LIST(INDEXES(_), _["_2"], _["tier"]))
--- expect
tree -{"1"=-{"1"=-{"1"=t"X", "2"=t"x", "3"=t"_1", "4"=t"Y", "5"=t"y", "6"=t"_2", "7"=t"k", "8"=t"tier"}, "2"=-{"id"=-, "sku"=-, "Y"=-, "y"=-}, "3"=t"L"}}
===
### name: rel.link-left.unmatched-left-fields-clash-with-the-null-record
--- note
The left element's fields are promoted when their names do not occur in the
right element -- for an unmatched row, the null record: `sku` does, `tier`
does not.
--- source
X = LIST(RECORD("k", 9, "sku", "L", "tier", "t")); Y = LIST(RECORD("id", 1, "sku", "s")); J = X .> LINK_LEFT(Y, _1["k"] == _2["id"]); J .> MAP(INDEXES(_))
--- expect
tree -{"1"=-{"1"=t"X", "2"=t"x", "3"=t"_1", "4"=t"Y", "5"=t"y", "6"=t"_2", "7"=t"k", "8"=t"tier"}}
===
### name: rel.link-left.empty-right-side-binds-the-name-keys
--- note
With no right elements the unmatched row's right binders hold a record of the
keys binding would add, the name and its lowercase, each NULL.
--- source
X = LIST(RECORD("k", 1, "a", 1)); Y = LIST(); J = X .> LINK_LEFT(Y, _1["k"] == _2["id"]); J .> MAP(LIST(INDEXES(_), _["_2"]))
--- expect
tree -{"1"=-{"1"=-{"1"=t"X", "2"=t"x", "3"=t"_1", "4"=t"Y", "5"=t"y", "6"=t"_2", "7"=t"k", "8"=t"a"}, "2"=-{"Y"=-, "y"=-}}}
===
### name: rel.link-left.mixed-matched-and-unmatched-rows
--- note
Matched and unmatched rows side by side, each promoted from its own pair.
--- source
X = LIST(RECORD("k", 1, "tier", "L1"), RECORD("k", 9, "name", "L2"), RECORD("k", 1, "sku", "L3")); Y = LIST(RECORD("id", 1, "tier", "R", "amt", 4)); J = X .> LINK_LEFT(Y, _1["k"] == _2["id"]); J .> MAP(INDEXES(_))
--- expect
tree -{"1"=-{"1"=t"X", "2"=t"x", "3"=t"_1", "4"=t"Y", "5"=t"y", "6"=t"_2", "7"=t"k", "8"=t"id", "9"=t"amt"}, "2"=-{"1"=t"X", "2"=t"x", "3"=t"_1", "4"=t"Y", "5"=t"y", "6"=t"_2", "7"=t"k", "8"=t"name"}, "3"=-{"1"=t"X", "2"=t"x", "3"=t"_1", "4"=t"Y", "5"=t"y", "6"=t"_2", "7"=t"k", "8"=t"sku", "9"=t"id", "10"=t"tier", "11"=t"amt"}}
===
### name: rel.link.chain.promotion.per-pair-at-each-join
--- note
Two joins over elements of different shapes: each row of the second join is
built from the first join's row it came from.
--- source
X = LIST(RECORD("k", 1, "a", 1), RECORD("k", 2, "b", 2)); Y = LIST(RECORD("id", 1, "k2", 1, "x", "x1"), RECORD("id", 2, "k2", 1, "y", "y2")); Z = LIST(RECORD("id", 1, "z", "z")); X .> LINK(Y, _1["k"] == _2["id"]) .> LINK(Z, _1["Y"]["k2"] == _2["id"]) .> MAP(INDEXES(_))
--- expect
tree -{"1"=-{"1"=t"X", "2"=t"x", "3"=t"_1", "4"=t"Y", "5"=t"y", "6"=t"_2", "7"=t"Z", "8"=t"z", "9"=t"k", "10"=t"a", "11"=t"k2"}, "2"=-{"1"=t"X", "2"=t"x", "3"=t"_1", "4"=t"Y", "5"=t"y", "6"=t"_2", "7"=t"Z", "8"=t"z", "9"=t"k", "10"=t"b", "11"=t"k2"}}
===
### name: rel.link.promotion.per-pair.five-argument-form
--- source
X = LIST(RECORD("k", 1, "a", 1), RECORD("k", 1, "b", 2)); Y = LIST(RECORD("id", 1, "c", 3)); LINK(X, Y, L, R, L["k"] == R["id"]) .> MAP(INDEXES(_))
--- expect
tree -{"1"=-{"1"=t"L", "2"=t"l", "3"=t"_1", "4"=t"R", "5"=t"r", "6"=t"_2", "7"=t"k", "8"=t"a", "9"=t"id", "10"=t"c"}, "2"=-{"1"=t"L", "2"=t"l", "3"=t"_1", "4"=t"R", "5"=t"r", "6"=t"_2", "7"=t"k", "8"=t"b", "9"=t"id", "10"=t"c"}}
===
### name: rel.link.promotion.per-pair.literal-sides
--- source
LIST(RECORD("k", 1, "a", 1), RECORD("k", 1, "b", 2)) .> LINK(LIST(RECORD("id", 1, "c", 3)), _1["k"] == _2["id"]) .> MAP(INDEXES(_))
--- expect
tree -{"1"=-{"1"=t"_1", "2"=t"_2", "3"=t"k", "4"=t"a", "5"=t"id", "6"=t"c"}, "2"=-{"1"=t"_1", "2"=t"_2", "3"=t"k", "4"=t"b", "5"=t"id", "6"=t"c"}}
===
### name: rel.link.binder.an-element-with-its-name-field-is-bound-as-it-is
--- note
The second right element has a field `Y` of its own: it is bound as it is,
with neither `Y` nor `y` added (§7.4); the first is extended as usual. The
joined row's binder keys still hold the element.
--- source
X = LIST(RECORD("k", 1)); Y = LIST(RECORD("id", 1, "n", 1), RECORD("id", 1, "Y", "own")); J = X .> LINK(Y, _1["k"] == _2["id"]); J .> MAP(LIST(INDEXES(_["_2"]), _["Y"]["id"]))
--- expect
tree -{"1"=-{"1"=-{"1"=t"id", "2"=t"n", "3"=t"Y", "4"=t"y"}, "2"=t"1"}, "2"=-{"1"=-{"1"=t"id", "2"=t"Y"}, "2"=t"1"}}
===
### name: rel.link.binder.the-lowercase-key-is-not-added-twice
--- note
A left element with a field `x` of its own gains `X` only: the lowercase is
added where the element has no such key.
--- source
X = LIST(RECORD("k", 1, "x", LIST(1))); Y = LIST(RECORD("id", 1)); J = X .> LINK(Y, _1["k"] == _2["id"]); J .> MAP(LIST(INDEXES(_["_1"]), INDEXES(_)))
--- expect
tree -{"1"=-{"1"=-{"1"=t"k", "2"=t"x", "3"=t"X"}, "2"=-{"1"=t"X", "2"=t"x", "3"=t"_1", "4"=t"Y", "5"=t"y", "6"=t"_2", "7"=t"k", "8"=t"id"}}}
===
### name: rel.link-left.null-record-of-an-element-bound-as-it-is
--- note
The first right element has its own `Y` and is bound unextended, so the null
record of an unmatched row has its keys and no `y`.
--- source
X = LIST(RECORD("k", 9)); Y = LIST(RECORD("id", 1, "Y", "own")); J = X .> LINK_LEFT(Y, _1["k"] == _2["id"]); J .> MAP(INDEXES(_["_2"]))
--- expect
tree -{"1"=-{"1"=t"id", "2"=t"Y"}}
===
### name: rel.link-left.empty-literal-right-side-binds-null
--- note
No right elements and no name: the unmatched row's right binder is NULL, and
every left field is promoted.
--- source
LIST(RECORD("k", 1, "a", 2)) .> LINK_LEFT(LIST(), _1["k"] == _2["id"]) .> MAP(LIST(INDEXES(_), _["_2"]))
--- expect
tree -{"1"=-{"1"=-{"1"=t"_1", "2"=t"_2", "3"=t"k", "4"=t"a"}, "2"=-}}
===
